    <summary>Application Server. Windows 64 bit only. Jakarta EE 11 implementation.</summary>
    <description>Apache Tomcat 11 is a web application server that implements Jakarta EE 11 specifications. Applications use the `jakarta.*` namespace, like Tomcat 10.

### Important Note
Apache only publishes 64 bit Windows binaries for Tomcat 11, so this package requires 64 bit Windows. Applications written for Tomcat 9 and earlier (`javax.*` namespace) require code changes to run on Tomcat 11. Apache provides a migration tool to assist with this transition.

### Prerequisite
* JDK (Java Development Kit) 17 or later is required. It was not listed as dependency, in order to support different variations of JDK.
* Environment variable `JAVA_HOME` needs to be set to a JDK path. Many JDK installers already do this for users.

### Usage
After installation, configuration and application data are installed in a folder named `Tomcat11`, which locates in `%ProgramData%` (or `%LocalAppData%` when admin right is not granted). The folder is supposed to be managed by user (site manager), and it will not be touched when this package gets upgraded or uninstalled.

If admin right is granted, a [service](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Windows_service) is installed with service name `Tomcat11` and display name beginning with "Apache Tomcat 11". It is neither started nor enabled (start on boot) by default. Services can be managed with a [MMC (Microsoft Management Console)](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Microsoft_Management_Console) snap-in, which can be accessed by running `services.msc`. In the snap-in the service can be started, stopped, and enabled on-boot. Please refer to third-party guides (such as [this one](https://www.thewindowsclub.com/open-windows-services)) for managing services on Windows.

### Side-by-Side Installation
This package can be installed alongside the `tomcat` package (Tomcat 9) and the `tomcat10` package. Each version uses separate directories and service names, allowing you to run several versions simultaneously on different ports.</description>
    <releaseNotes>https://tomcat.apache.org/tomcat-11.0-doc/changelog.html</releaseNotes>
